        />
        <span class="zoomable__hint" aria-hidden="true">Tap to zoom</span>
      </button>
      <figcaption>
        The response blueprint: calories, macros, spike risk and a metabolic verdict, always
        ending on the likely sugar spike.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="killed">
      <div class="killed__text">
        <span class="killed__tag">Shelved: the Meal Score</span>
        <p class="killed__lead">What we shipped instead</p>
        <p>
          The richer the insight, the longer the model takes to answer. A person holding their
          phone after a meal will not wait. So the card based breakdown and the Meal Score were
          set aside and we shipped clean text and tables instead, which also saved real
          development effort. Shipping something people could use beat polishing something they
          could not.
        </p>
      </div>
      <button
        class="zoomable killed__shot"
