    {/* 12. GIVING KAIRA AN IDENTITY */}
    <div class="identity">
    <section class="beat">
      <h2 class="beat__h">Giving Kaira an identity</h2>
      <p>
        A chatbot needs a name and a face. I worked with marketing to define what Kaira should
        be: knowledgeable but never clinical, clearly a part of GoodFlip but distinct enough that
        people know when they are talking to AI. The name came out of that: Kaira, Knowledgeable
        AI for Remission and Awareness.
      </p>
    </section>

    <ol class="idtl">
      <li class="idtl__stage">
        <span class="idtl__num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <h3 class="idtl__label">What AI looks like today</h3>
        <p class="idtl__line">
          Jakob's law cuts both ways. I looked at how AI presents itself across products and
          found simple shapes with gradients. People already know what AI looks like, so the mark
          had to be recognisable before it was clever.
        </p>
        <figure class="idtl__visual">
          <Image src={kairaLogoLandscape} alt="Competitive analysis grid of AI product logos" widths={[600, 1000]} sizes="(max-width: 44rem) 92vw, 38rem" />
