    {/* 13. LEARNINGS */}
    <section class="beat">
      <p class="beat__eyebrow">Ship it, then let the data prove me wrong</p>
      <h2 class="beat__h">Learnings</h2>
      <p>
        Six weeks after launch I audited 4,000 conversations across 168 users, and read them
        against what I had assumed while designing.
      </p>
      <p class="honesty-line">
        Sources: MoEngage events, full conversation logs, and AI driven feedback calls so I could
        hear people in their own words. March 11 to 31, 2026.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="findings">
      <div class="finding">
        <h3 class="finding__h">The bet on curiosity paid off.</h3>
        <p>
          I had designed Kaira as a surface, not a feature, on the assumption that people would
          want more from her than a calorie count. They did.
        </p>
        <div class="finding__stat">
          <span class="finding__fig">28%</span>
          <div class="finding__statbody">
            <span class="finding__label">of conversations went beyond logging, with people asking about their meals, their spikes and what to do next.</span>
            <span class="text-ph finding__base">base to confirm: conversations, users, or messages, and the date range</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="finding">
        <h3 class="finding__h">The data corrected me.</h3>
        <p>
          I built for voice. People reached for text first and the camera second, with voice the
          smallest of the three. The input I centred the design on was the one people wanted
          least.
        </p>
        {/* VIZ-07 — input mode split */}
        <div class="viz viz07">
          <div class="viz07__bar viz07__bar--text" style="width: 100%;"><span>Text</span></div>
          <div class="viz07__bar viz07__bar--camera" style="width: 62%;"><span>Camera</span></div>
          <div class="viz07__bar viz07__bar--voice" style="width: 28%;"><span>Voice</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="viz__cap">the input I designed for</p>
      </div>

      <div class="finding">
        <h3 class="finding__h">Waiting is the new friction.</h3>
        <p>
          Kaira still takes too long to answer. Speed is part of the fix, but the better answer is
          to remove the wait rather than shorten it, because a person holding their phone after a
          meal has no reason to wait for anything.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="finding finding--double">
        <h3 class="finding__h">The habit is real, but small.</h3>
        <p>
          Of everyone on GoodFlip, fewer than <span class="text-ph">10%</span> log their food, up
          from under <span class="text-ph">2%</span> before Kaira (to reconcile against the 3.7%,
          256 of 6,866 over 60 days, figure if it is the same measure). Of the people who do log,
          about 9 in 10 now do it on their own. The behaviour changed. The reach has not caught up
          yet.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="beat">
      <p class="beat__lead">
        That last number is the one I would lead with in a review. We proved people will log
        without being pushed. We have not yet given most of them a reason to start.
      </p>
    </section>

